From 33ac9c6632b6206f49cabfca97763ced598011be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Chen <rchen14b@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Mar 2026 16:23:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] airoha: enable bridge offload for AN7581 target

Enable L2 bridge hardware flow offloading on AN7581 using the
bridge-family flowtable from the 675 patch series (no kmod-br-netfilter).

Add bridge-flow-offload package:
  - Detects bridge member ports dynamically from /sys/class/net/br-lan/brif
  - Generates a bridge-family nftables flowtable and forward-chain rule in
    /usr/share/nftables.d/ruleset-post/30-bridge-offload.nft
  - Triggers fw4 reload to apply the ruleset-post include
  - DEPENDS: kmod-nft-bridge, firewall4

Add iface hotplug script (51-bridge-flow-offload) that fires on ifup of
the lan interface with a 10-second settle time, allowing WiFi AP
interfaces to join br-lan before bridge port detection. Uses flock to
serialize concurrent events.

The bridge-family flowtable itself is provided by kmod-nft-offload
(nf_flow_table_inet.ko), which registers the NFPROTO_BRIDGE flowtable
type per the 675 patch series; it is pulled in transitively via
firewall4, so no separate kmod is needed.

Add bridge-flow-offload to DEFAULT_PACKAGES in target.mk so it is
included in all images.

Assisted-By: OpenCode <assist@opencode.ai>
Signed-off-by: Ryan Chen <rchen14b@gmail.com>
